  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Exploration of the Dutch biomethane value chain by Naftogaz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity facilitates a visit by Naftogaz, Ukraine&apos;s largest national oil and gas company, to the Netherlands to explore the biomethane value chain. As a key player in Ukraine&apos;s energy sector, Naftogaz aims to transition toward greener energy solutions in alignment with the country&apos;s energy transition goals. The visit includes meetings with Dutch stakeholders such as Gasunie, Host Energy, and STX Group, focusing on best practices, infrastructure design, regulatory frameworks, and financing opportunities. By gaining expertise in biomethane production and its integration into existing systems, Naftogaz seeks to reduce Ukraine&#x2019;s dependence on natural gas, promote sustainable energy practices, and contribute to the European Union (EU)&#x2019;s RePower EU targets. This initiative also strengthens partnerships between Dutch and Ukrainian energy stakeholders, supporting climate mitigation and the global energy transition.</narrative>
  </description>
